# Credit Cards Module

## Scope

Philippine bank credit card SOA automation. This module must preserve behavior from `automated-tasks/pay-credit-cards` unless explicitly changing product requirements.

## Supported Banks

Card create/edit lists **e-wallets that issue credit cards** (Maya), plus the same Philippine **digital banks** and **traditional banks** as Kame Homes payment providers. Existing issuer IDs (`metrobank`, `rcbc`, `bpi`, `unionbank`) are unchanged.

| Issuer ID | Label | Gmail SOA notes |
| --------- | ----- | ---------------- |
| `maya` | Maya | Billing-statement subject phrase; received-date window (periods are `YYYY-MM-DD`). Security-deposit mail excluded. Parse reads billing date, due/total pair, minimum, and `Description amount DD Mon DD Mon` rows from the text layer (summary labels are vectors) |

Dedicated SOA parsers:

| Issuer ID | Label | Notes |
| --------- | ----- | ----- |
| `metrobank` | Metrobank | MSOA / SOA Gmail queries |
| `rcbc` | RCBC | FLEX VISA; geometry-ordered PDF lines |
| `bpi` | BPI | Often needs OCR (auto-detected; `BPI_OCR` forces it) |
| `unionbank` | Unionbank | REWARDS VISA patterns |

Other issuers (BDO, Security Bank, PNB, GoTyme, etc.) can be registered, get due-day reminders, and use generic Gmail subject search + generic parse / AI extract / manual upload. Catalog: `PH_BANK_ISSUERS` in `lib/db/schema/credit-cards.ts`.

## SOA Pipeline (service layer)

Order of operations (`lib/soa/run.ts`):

1. Build month context (`gmailMonthOffset` per card)
2. Gmail search per bank → download PDFs
3. Unlock PDF with card password(s)
4. Assess extracted text quality (`lib/soa/text-quality.ts`); auto-OCR fallback
   (`lib/soa/pdf-ocr.ts`) for **any** issuer when text looks unusable. Box-drawing
   section rules (UnionBank `─` lines) are dividers, so that text layer is kept.
   RCBC total due is the amount beside `MINIMUM PAYMENT DUE`, not the largest
   nearby figure (spend-analyzer year-to-date). Override via
   `SOA_OCR_FORCE` / `SOA_OCR_DISABLE` (`lib/soa/ocr-env.ts`); legacy `BPI_OCR*` are
   BPI-only aliases. On Vercel, Tesseract WASM is vendored by `prepare-server-native`
   and OCR is time-capped so a missing core cannot stall the run.
5. Parse SOA fields + transactions
6. Upsert `due_entries` via `due-entry-upsert.service`
7. Write summary PDF (paid column from Postgres via `overview-paid-label`)
8. Notify via `notification.service` (Telegram PDF + Slack text)
9. Optional: calendar events via `google-calendar.service` → `lib/soa/google-calendar.ts`

**Re-run** can set `skipExistingCards` (UI default on). Cards with a real statement for that month are not searched or parsed again. Cards without one still run, and Telegram, Slack, and Calendar still apply to new statements.

## Due Entries

- Key: `issuerId` + normalized `cardLast4` + `dueDateYmd`
- Keep latest due date when range runs overlap
- `paidAt` suppresses reminder fingerprints
- `overviewIsPaidLabel` → `lib/soa/overview-paid-label.ts` (Postgres `due_entries`)

## Mark Paid

| Input | Behavior |
| ----- | -------- |
| `xxxx - month year - paid` | Text command (Telegram or API) |
| Receipt image | AI vision → amount recorded. One file records that payment. Several files ask whether they are one payment or separate payments. Separate payments sum. One payment counts the set once. Marks paid when the minimum or total due is met |
| `xxxx - month year - unpaid` | Reverse paid state |

Side effects: update due entry, suppress/restore reminder fingerprints, patch calendar events.

## Receipt AI validation

- Gemini 2.5 Flash vision (multi-key rotation) + Groq fallback
- API keys: **Settings only** (`ai_api_keys` table) — never `GEMINI_*` / `GROQ_*` env vars
- Extract card last-4, amount, bank/wallet from PH e-wallet/bank screenshots
- Amount must meet minimum due (or total when `RECEIPT_REQUIRE_TOTAL_DUE=1`) to mark paid and silence reminders; partial amounts are saved and summed across receipts until threshold is met
- **Add receipt** on a receipts card passes that statement’s due entry. Later files stay on that bank and month after the due is already paid. A separate-payment upload adds each amount. A one-payment upload counts that set once. The page-level upload keeps matching a card on its own and leaves a fully paid due unchanged
- Several files in one upload ask **One payment** or **Separate payments** on Receipts, Reminders, and an SOA period. One file skips the choice
- Same card and statement period display as one receipt card. The viewer pages through each image
- Store uploads in Supabase Storage under `receipts/{userId}/`

## Security

- Card PDF passwords: encrypt at rest; never return in API responses
- Gmail/Calendar tokens: per-user integration record, not global `.env` files in production

## Testing Parity

When porting parsers, compare output against legacy CLI on sample PDFs in `pay-credit-cards/data/downloads/`.

## Skills

Use `/credit-cards` and `/integrations` skills when implementing this module.
